{
 "note": "each moving spar (docs/shipkit-3): origin_m on the axis it turns about (metres, ship frame) and that axis (the object's local +Z); parent, the object it rides on; hoist_m, its offset along the axis [lowered, hoisted] (negative is down; the model hangs it hoisted); brace_deg, the limits of a turn about local +Z (right-handed: positive swings a square yard's starboard arm aft and the spanker boom and gaff to port); port_tack_sign, the sign of the turn that trims it for the wind on the port side (each yard's lee arm aft, the boom and gaff to leeward). Since slice 4 the limits are the standing rigging's: brace_deg is the hoisted part's, brace_deg_by_hoist [hoist, lo, hi] the limits from lowered (0) to hoisted (1) (between two, take the smaller); each is the last clear angle less 1 deg. ease_m [[deg, m]] (lower and topsail yards, hoisted): as it braces, a yard's truss or parrel lets it come forward: move its origin along its own +X by the table's value at |brace| (interpolated), then turn it. ease_m_by_hoist [[hoist, [[deg, m]]]] (topsail yards): the same table at each hoist; between two hoists, interpolate between their tables' values",
